A||N||5||polomeno||Parking brake cables||||11||
Z||000000||polomeno||06-17-2000||05:04 PM||||Hey, i was about to change the parking brake cable on my 84 coupe and i wanted to know if i have to buy specific cables for this car or are there others that will work... cause it is a huge pain in the ass in my city to get parts for a 84 fiero..<BR>thanks for any help||||reg||11
Z||000001||2birds||06-17-2000||06:03 PM||||Before you drop the cash for them, make sure the rear brake recall was done on yours. 86-C-16 is  the recall #.  They replaced my e-brake cables as part of the recall work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||06-17-2000||06:08 PM||||Where do i look for that # ??  and how od i know if the work was already done or not?<BR>i have a 84 sport coupe<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||84 Indy||06-17-2000||07:11 PM||||Look on the internet under automotive recalls<BR>check out consumer affairs the NHTSB has listed all recalls. there are 3 for the 84 fiero. I have an appointment thursday an pontiac for a recall inspection. None were done. if you have a 4cyl there was also a recall for connecting rods.  My dealer told me that if the recall was not done he would have to put a new motor in. As far as telling what recalls were done there should be a sticker by the emissions sticker with the campigan number on it||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||06-18-2000||01:00 AM||||The dealer can run your VIN through a computer and see all work ever done by a GM dealership, after a certain year (unsure of when, though).  Some recalls have ending dates, too, so I don't know if this one is still active (mine was done in 95).  They also register the recalls done on each car (by VIN) as they are done, with corporate headquarters.  I think you can still also call 1-800-PM-CARES for info.  I didn't find out about the brake recall until after I rebuilt my calipers.  They still leaked from the check valve, so I took it to the dealer.  New pistons (minus the check valve) are installed to prevent the leak, they will replace pads damaged by brake fluid, and they can change the cables if needed.  My calipers still stuck after they did the pistons, so they replaced my cables, too.<P><BR>Sorry, I was just reminded on the the other e-brake post that this recall only applies to manual tranny cars.   Hope yours is one of the lucky ones.<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 06-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Majik||06-19-2000||07:38 PM||||Actually, the dealer can't find information on anything before 86 (got this info from my local dealer).  I even called Pontiac and their records only go back 5 years.  <BR>The campaign stickers will be placed under the deck lid.<BR>Even though they couldn't bump my VIN through their computers, they are still doing the engine fire campagin on the car...so they are a bit more lax than I thought since they couldn't bump the VIN.<P>Hope this helps...and good luck!||||reg||1
